    "id": "rate_half_list_budget_three_fiber_two_cycle_boundary_transfer",
    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two cycle boundaries transfer through canonical span",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For every c=0,1,2 fiber-two cycle quartic-pencil stratum at quotient order 2^40, all parameter-uniform boundary theorems transfer through the canonical-span certifier. The generic and intermediate minimum-degree boundaries both have linear differential residual and the same primary gap a_(2^38)=a_(2^38+1)=0, a_(2^38+2)!=0; the generic secondary gaps are at 2^37-1 and 2^37. A two-antipodal-pair denominator uses M=2^36. The canonical outer quartic must be PGL-matched to the cycle completion roots rho_i. Only at c=0 are these automatically square-root lifts of all denominator roots, so the old one-parameter Mobius-ratio/norm gates are not imported into c=1,2.",
